00:45:29.190 --> 00:45:30.790
So I have two comments.

00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:33.990
The first comment is that my colleagues

00:45:33.990 --> 00:45:37.370
at NYU have published a paper
that you cite in your paper

00:45:37.370 --> 00:45:39.530
about why leaders visit other countries.

00:45:39.530 --> 00:45:41.900
And I know this paper well

00:45:41.900 --> 00:45:43.810
and they sort of make this claim

00:45:43.810 --> 00:45:46.640
that if a foreign leader
visits another country

00:45:46.640 --> 00:45:48.850
it sends a signal that they expect

00:45:48.850 --> 00:45:52.270
that the incumbent and the
other country will be in power

00:45:52.270 --> 00:45:54.450
for the foreseeable future.

00:45:54.450 --> 00:45:56.730
So a visit from a foreign leader

00:45:56.730 --> 00:46:01.560
can help to prevent domestic
opponents and the host country

00:46:01.560 --> 00:46:04.020
from attacking the incumbent
or criticizing the incumbent

00:46:04.020 --> 00:46:05.890
and trying to depose the incumbent.

00:46:05.890 --> 00:46:07.340
So this suggests

00:46:07.340 --> 00:46:09.510
I was just thinking
about for your project.

00:46:09.510 --> 00:46:11.300
It suggests that, you know, leader visits,

00:46:11.300 --> 00:46:14.330
I mean you're not saying that
that random, but it suggests

00:46:14.330 --> 00:46:17.440
that leader visits may
be more about the need

00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:20.320
