00:46:59.420 --> 00:47:01.000
but instead it's do you approve

00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:04.760
or disapprove of the job
performance of the foreign leader?

00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:07.343
And that just like, that seems a little,

00:47:08.600 --> 00:47:11.450
like people don't have views
often of the job performance

00:47:11.450 --> 00:47:15.030
of their own leaders, let alone, you know,

00:47:15.030 --> 00:47:19.140
the views of use of the job
performance of foreign leaders.

00:47:19.140 --> 00:47:22.340
So I'm just wondering if
this is a situation where

00:47:22.340 --> 00:47:23.530
you know, you never see,

00:47:23.530 --> 00:47:25.500
so like the public in the United States

00:47:25.500 --> 00:47:28.970
never see Stephen Harper doing his job

00:47:28.970 --> 00:47:31.730
and then suddenly they see
Stephen Harper doing his job

00:47:31.730 --> 00:47:36.270
by visiting their leader,
and like shaking hands.

00:47:36.270 --> 00:47:38.020
And I'm just wondering
if this is more like

00:47:38.020 --> 00:47:40.410
people don't have information,
so they are indifferent

00:47:40.410 --> 00:47:42.310
and then they move
toward having information

00:47:42.310 --> 00:47:45.510
which induces a positive attitude.

00:47:45.510 --> 00:47:47.837
And your results same know
consistent with, you know,

00:47:47.837 --> 00:47:50.949
there's evidence that it's indifference

00:47:50.949 --> 00:47:53.330
moving to lessen difference

00:47:53.330 --> 00:47:56.470
rather than people holding
kind of negative views.

00:47:56.470 --> 00:48:00.020
But I just wanted to raise
those two points, but overall

00:48:00.020 --> 00:48:02.020
it's a really great
paper and I enjoyed it.

00:48:02.020 --> 00:48:05.520
And I really enjoyed seeing
that picture of Yakiniku.

00:48:05.520 --> 00:48:06.540
Thank you.

00:48:06.540 --> 00:48:09.443
I'm feeling quite
depressed right now, but.

00:48:11.920 --> 00:48:13.450
- I think I'm next.

00:48:13.450 --> 00:48:15.280
So I also enjoyed this paper a lot

00:48:15.280 --> 00:48:19.310
and I think it's a really cool
approach to this question.

00:48:19.310 --> 00:48:20.960
So two points.

00:48:20.960 --> 00:48:24.660
So the first is about the
kind of substantive conclusion

00:48:25.849 --> 00:48:30.250
and just think looking at
this from an IR perspective,

00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:34.150
I didn't really buy the
idea that, you know,

00:48:34.150 --> 00:48:37.310
this is sort of a
substantively important effect

00:48:37.310 --> 00:48:39.090
which is not to subtract from the paper.

00:48:39.090 --> 00:48:42.130
I think the paper is fine,
but kind of framing this

00:48:42.130 --> 00:48:44.440
as a sort of an important, big effect,

00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:46.290
I felt like didn't sit well with me.

00:48:46.290 --> 00:48:48.750
So it's basically a 2% change

00:48:48.750 --> 00:48:53.010
in the public opinion of a
foreign country for 20 days.

00:48:53.010 --> 00:48:56.530
And so, you know, that
kind of magnitude of change

00:48:56.530 --> 00:48:59.660
could matter if you're
running a domestic election

00:48:59.660 --> 00:49:02.250
with a certain kind of electoral rule,

00:49:02.250 --> 00:49:05.860
but it's the foreign citizenry, you know

00:49:05.860 --> 00:49:07.450
and that marginal difference

00:49:07.450 --> 00:49:09.650
is really not gonna have an impact

00:49:09.650 --> 00:49:13.760
on any kind of policy
outcome that we care about.

00:49:13.760 --> 00:49:15.610
And so to me, this, the punchline here

00:49:15.610 --> 00:49:17.510
is it does have an effect

00:49:17.510 --> 00:49:20.320
but it's not really gonna
matter for anything.

00:49:20.320 --> 00:49:23.190
And I think that's still
fine in terms of the paper

00:49:23.190 --> 00:49:24.790
because you're measuring something

00:49:24.790 --> 00:49:27.710
and it might have other important effects,

00:49:27.710 --> 00:49:30.800
but I didn't quite agree

00:49:30.800 --> 00:49:34.043
with the way the paper
was framing the findings.

00:49:35.247 --> 00:49:37.610
And the second one was
Christina's comment.

00:49:37.610 --> 00:49:39.360
I think very similar

00:49:39.360 --> 00:49:43.430
but the appendix K
coding of the the visits

00:49:43.430 --> 00:49:47.040
they came with sort of a policy outcome

00:49:47.040 --> 00:49:49.310
struck me as maybe being too strict.

00:49:49.310 --> 00:49:52.550
Like, it seems like just subjectively look

00:49:52.550 --> 00:49:54.930
