00:50:21.340 --> 00:50:22.620
that's coming out of the meeting.

00:50:22.620 --> 00:50:25.378
And so I worried a little bit there.

00:50:25.378 --> 00:50:27.150
And so it might be
worth talking, you know,

00:50:27.150 --> 00:50:28.853
there are visits like that,

00:50:30.430 --> 00:50:33.460
but it left me with some questions.

00:50:33.460 --> 00:50:36.270
And so maybe that could
be addressed as well.

00:50:36.270 --> 00:50:38.160
I have some more stuff
that I'll send separately.

00:50:38.160 --> 00:50:39.410
A great paper, thank you.

00:50:42.190 --> 00:50:43.703
- Great, Mike Thomas is next.

00:50:44.570 --> 00:50:47.160
- Great, well, I thought this
was just a fascinating paper.

00:50:47.160 --> 00:50:48.500
I learned a lot from reading it.

00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:50.800
It was very thought provoking.

00:50:50.800 --> 00:50:52.250
I have a bunch of comments,

00:50:52.250 --> 00:50:53.700
but I'm gonna just give you

00:50:53.700 --> 00:50:55.430
kind of two clusters of comments,

00:50:55.430 --> 00:50:59.730
one about moderators and
one about treatments.

00:50:59.730 --> 00:51:02.680
So my moderator's comment is an effort,

00:51:02.680 --> 00:51:05.580
I think to connect the two
papers on today's panel

00:51:07.040 --> 00:51:09.720
by suggesting that a key moderator

00:51:09.720 --> 00:51:11.960
that's maybe not explored
in this paper so far

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:14.610
is the politicization of a diet.

00:51:14.610 --> 00:51:18.710
So if the first paper on
today's panel is correct,

00:51:18.710 --> 00:51:20.530
then efforts to increase soft power

00:51:20.530 --> 00:51:22.740
including by diplomatic visits

00:51:22.740 --> 00:51:25.730
should depend on whether
the dyadic relationship

00:51:25.730 --> 00:51:27.750
between the countries
is politicized or not

00:51:27.750 --> 00:51:29.080
one way that you could test that

00:51:29.080 --> 00:51:32.713
would be by estimating
preexisting levels of hostility

00:51:35.100 --> 00:51:37.500
and or favoritism between the countries

00:51:37.500 --> 00:51:39.330
and or with the public opinion data.

00:51:39.330 --> 00:51:41.930
You have looking at the
pre-visit popularity

00:51:41.930 --> 00:51:45.770
of the foreign leader as a
measure of the moderator.

00:51:45.770 --> 00:51:47.380
But let me deepen that point a little bit,

00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:49.010
because I worry that your estimates

00:51:49.010 --> 00:51:51.030
are probably an upper bound

00:51:51.030 --> 00:51:54.550
on the positive effects of diplomacy.

00:51:54.550 --> 00:51:56.560
You describe what you're doing

00:51:56.560 --> 00:51:58.730
in the study as a natural experiment.

00:51:58.730 --> 00:52:01.270
And I guess at some level

00:52:01.270 --> 00:52:04.040
whether respondent
answers the survey before

00:52:04.040 --> 00:52:07.170
or after the visit is as if random

00:52:07.170 --> 00:52:11.030
but the thing that's not
random is the visit itself.

00:52:11.030 --> 00:52:15.110
Guests have to be invited
and guests have to accept.

00:52:15.110 --> 00:52:18.100
So let's suppose that
guests who aren't welcome,

00:52:18.100 --> 00:52:21.020
won't be invited and let's
suppose that guests who think

00:52:21.020 --> 00:52:23.440
that their visit might
not help or might backfire

00:52:23.440 --> 00:52:26.220
probably won't accept the invitation.

00:52:26.220 --> 00:52:27.810
Then those two things are going to limit

00:52:27.810 --> 00:52:31.130
the general liability of your findings.

00:52:31.130 --> 00:52:34.410
It's as if the subset of the visits

00:52:34.410 --> 00:52:36.900
that we actually observe our best cases

00:52:36.900 --> 00:52:39.200
for a positive effect of diplomacy.

00:52:39.200 --> 00:52:41.247
So, anyway that's my attempt

00:52:41.247 --> 00:52:43.060
to connect the two papers together.

00:52:43.060 --> 00:52:46.530
My second comment is about
what counts as a treatment.

00:52:46.530 --> 00:52:49.210
And I guess I have two
small things to say here

00:52:49.210 --> 00:52:53.290
but one builds on something
that Michael already mentioned

00:52:53.290 --> 00:52:55.790
because he was wondering
what counts as a treatment

00:52:55.790 --> 00:52:58.453
the first day of the actual
visit or something else.

00:52:59.570 --> 00:53:01.070
I have two suggestions there.

00:53:01.070 --> 00:53:03.810
One would be to actually study the effects

00:53:03.810 --> 00:53:06.760
of pre-visit publicity, if you can.

00:53:06.760 --> 00:53:08.240
And the second would be to point out

00:53:08.240 --> 00:53:10.700
that given the methods that you use

00:53:10.700 --> 00:53:14.660
any pre-visit publicity effects
are gonna make it harder

00:53:14.660 --> 00:53:17.890
for you to detect the
effect of an actual visit.

00:53:17.890 --> 00:53:20.100
So to the extent that there's
bias in the estimates,

00:53:20.100 --> 00:53:21.840
the bias is gonna be against

00:53:21.840 --> 00:53:24.620
finding an effect on the day of the visit.

00:53:24.620 --> 00:53:27.400
And so even if you can't study it,

00:53:27.400 --> 00:53:29.460
you can at least sign the bias

00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:33.850
caused by not being able to
consider those types of effects.

00:53:33.850 --> 00:53:35.460
The other thing that I was puzzled to buy

00:53:35.460 --> 00:53:37.990
and the treatments is that you find

00:53:37.990 --> 00:53:40.570
it's based on the graph that
the peak impact of a visit

00:53:40.570 --> 00:53:43.860
occurred around 15 or
16 days after the visit

00:53:43.860 --> 00:53:46.900
and then declined very
sharply in the next five days.

00:53:46.900 --> 00:53:49.220
So my question for you is what theory

00:53:49.220 --> 00:53:51.750
of persistence and decay

00:53:51.750 --> 00:53:54.240
could actually explain
that kind of pattern

00:53:54.240 --> 00:53:56.310
if, for example, the effects persisted

00:53:56.310 --> 00:53:58.430
because they learned something
about the foreign leader,

00:53:58.430 --> 00:54:00.300
then why would they dissipate so sharply

00:54:00.300 --> 00:54:03.460
within five days after
day 16, for example.

00:54:03.460 --> 00:54:06.440
So I'm a little bit of thinking
about pretreatment effects

00:54:06.440 --> 00:54:08.380
but also about the post-treatment effects

00:54:08.380 --> 00:54:10.790
and how those could be
theoretically motivated

00:54:10.790 --> 00:54:11.860
I think would help strengthen

00:54:11.860 --> 00:54:14.820
what's already an
excellent paper, thank you.

